@@ -105,3 +105,10 @@ Risks seen before the harness:
 - full-gate: Not in any gate: tools/test-integration.py and the other Python tools (they need a running server), and tests on MySQL, PostgreSQL or SQL Server (unit tests use H2 or memory only). Recorded in docs/harness/log.md.
 - local-env: debug.xml points web.path to ./traccar-web/simple, and the server stops at startup when that folder is missing (the submodule is empty in this checkout). make dev works around it with an API-only run (CONFIG_USE_ENVIRONMENT_VARIABLES=true, WEB_PATH=./target/web). The web UI cannot be served locally until the submodule question is answered.
 - fast-gate: This machine has only JDK 17 (default) and Homebrew JDK 25. The gates were verified on JDK 25 through tools/harness/java-home.sh. CI uses Temurin 21. Every Gradle run also needs Maven Central, because build.gradle resolves versions at configuration time.
+
+## 2026-11-02: JMAK CAN fields 15 to 38 and fuel unit
+
+- Changed: `JmakProtocolDecoder.decodeCan` now decodes CAN bits 15 to 38 (tripFuelUsed to instantFuelConsumption; engine load uses `Position.KEY_ENGINE_LOAD`). Bit 7 (fuel unit) is read instead of skipped: unit absent or "L" stores bit 8 as `fuel` (liters), any other unit stores it as `fuelLevel` (percentage).
+- Tests: `JmakProtocolDecoderTest.testDecodeCanExtendedFields` covers all 24 new fields and both fuel unit cases. The CAN values are synthetic (built from the field order), not a device capture; replace them with a real message when one is available.
+- Gates: `make test TESTS=org.traccar.protocol.JmakProtocolDecoderTest` passes (2 tests); `make check-fast` passes (613 tests, 0 failures, 27 skipped, Checkstyle clean).
+- Left: no real device sample with these fields; `make check` not run; the new attribute names are the ones given in the task, not checked against any device documentation.
